 "name": "Phase-field Bubbles 4: mixed foam",
 "description": "Big, medium and small bubbles from stamps of different sizes (the same content concentration, so size follows stamp: area in proportion to content). Bubbles eat a substrate fed in from outside and an edge needs it to advance, so between two neighbours, where it's eaten from both sides, both edges hold back: they keep a gap (23 stamped, 22 left at 40k steps). Try cutting one in two with Erase: the halves round up and stay two. Work in progress: crammed tighter (more content), pressure beats the starving and they merge. View u to see the substrate.",
